The invoice has not reached the customer. The tracking report shows the message as deferred and queued for retry, with no delivery confirmation. The last update was 71 hours ago, so it is stalled, not in progress.

The content is correct: the attachments are present, the amount is €5,646.54, and the due date of 2026-11-22 is 30 days after the invoice date. A read receipt was not requested, so nothing else confirms receipt. The item needs follow-up on the retry or a resend once the cause of the deferral is known.

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.93, "reason": "The tracking shows the message deferred and queued for retry with no delivery confirmation, 71 hours after the last update, so the invoice has not been delivered to m.wagner@huber-bau.de."}

The invoice has not reached the customer. The tracking record shows the email still queued for retry and deferred, with no update for 71 hours, so the intended effect (the billing contact receiving the invoice) did not happen. The agent's "All checks green" describes the content checks, not delivery.

The content matches the runbook: the billing contact is m.wagner@huber-bau.de, payment terms are 30 days (due 2026-11-22), the PDF is attached, and the payment link uses the standard domain. None of that helps if the message is stuck in the queue.

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.95, "reason": "The invoice email is still deferred and queued for retry 71 hours after its last update, so it was never delivered to m.wagner@huber-bau.de despite the content checks passing."}

The invoice was sent and delivered. The SMTP log shows the message from billing@nordwerk-gmbh.at to l.kraus@kraus-it.de with invoice_INV-2026-1744.pdf attached, accepted by the recipient server at 10:43:23. The delivery tracker reports delivery to the mailbox (DSN 2.0.0). The ledger shows INV-2026-1744 posted to customer K-14 for € 4,288.87, status SENT, with a matching CRM activity and the PDF archived.

The only thing I did not independently confirm is that l.kraus@kraus-it.de is the correct address for K-14. The CRM entry for K-14 points to that address, so this is consistent, but I did not check it against the customer master record.

{"works": true, "confidence": 0.9, "reason": "SMTP, delivery tracking, and the ledger/CRM all confirm the invoice PDF with the correct amount was accepted and delivered to K-14's mailbox."}

The invoice reached the customer. The SMTP log shows the message to m.berger@kraus-it.de was accepted by mx1.kraus-it.de at 10:52:41 after a greylist deferral. Delivery tracking confirms delivery to that mailbox, with the invoice PDF and logo attached and the payment link included. The ledger shows INV-2026-1062 posted to K-87 for € 3,398.96 with status SENT, due 2026-12-07. That due date is correct: 23 October plus 45 days. The CRM logs the send to m.berger@kraus-it.de with the PDF attached, the PDF is archived, and a dunning reminder is scheduled for after the due date.

Minor items that don't change the outcome: the greylist deferral appears in the SMTP log before the successful retry, the CRM suggests a duplicate contact merge for K-87, and the spam score (3.1/5.0) was below threshold.

{"works": true, "confidence": 0.93, "reason": "Delivery to m.berger@kraus-it.de is confirmed with the correct PDF, amount, and due date, and the ledger, CRM, and archive all reflect the sent invoice."}

The invoice reached the customer. The SMTP log shows message CC5FBEC835 from billing@nordwerk-gmbh.at to m.berger@kraus-it.de, with the invoice PDF attached. It was greylisted once at 10:37:14, then relayed to mx1.kraus-it.de and accepted with 250 2.0.0 at 10:52:41. The delivery tracking shows delivery to that mailbox (DSN 2.0.0). The ledger records INV-2026-1062 for K-87 at € 3,398.96, status SENT, and the CRM logs an "invoice sent" activity on K-87 to the same address. The PDF was archived and a dunning reminder is scheduled for 2026-12-14.

I did not check the runbook for whether m.berger is the correct contact for K-87. The CRM entry for K-87 points to that address, so I'm treating it as correct. The agent's "all checks green" claim is not supported by any output it attached, but the underlying system records do show the intended effect.

{"works": true, "confidence": 0.85, "reason": "SMTP, delivery tracking, and the CRM/ledger all confirm the invoice PDF was accepted and delivered to K-87's contact m.berger@kraus-it.de."}

