The work did not achieve its intended effect. The job log shows an inner merge with `respondents_meta.csv` that took the data from 9,160 rows to 1,770, dropping 7,390 respondents. The work item allowed only the 136 duplicates to be removed, so the output is missing about 80% of the valid respondents.

The weights were also rescaled to the 2,231,360 target over the 1,770 surviving rows, so the weighting is built on the wrong base. The validation report's "row count: 1,770 (raw 9,296, duplicates removed 136)" passes only because it checks against the post-merge count and never reconciles the 7,390-row gap. The "all checks green" claim does not account for this loss.

