The checks still pass, but they don't catch this. The weights sum to 2,231,360 only because they were rescaled over the 1,770 survivors, so the weight-total check hides the loss. The duplicate removal itself was correct (136 dropped, 1,770 unique IDs), and the 32-column schema is intact. The data is still unusable as the clean D1 dataset, because about 81% of valid respondents are missing and the weights now represent only the merged subset.

